#: processes/initialize-harness.bpmn:78
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Performed against the data store — a git repository, through the git CLI or a forge API. The instructions are at a PREDETERMINED spot on the harness: `<name>/docs/bootstrap/initialization.md`, the same for every harness, which is what lets a Bootstrapping Agent be pointed at one nobody has written yet."
msgstr ""

#: processes/initialize-harness.bpmn:77
#. Diagram label
msgid "Read the harness's declaration and instructions"
msgstr ""

#: processes/initialize-harness.bpmn:61
#. Diagram label
msgid "Read what each location already is"
msgstr ""

#: processes/initialize-harness.bpmn:90
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "REQUIRED logging, which is what drawing the call says. Logged before anything is written, so an install interrupted halfway is distinguishable from one never begun."
msgstr ""

#: processes/initialize-harness.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The candidates are listed and the Requestor is asked, in `discussion`, which asks through `human-agent-discussion`. IN: nothing but the context this agent was handed. OUT: zero or ONE harness, and the locations — a document conforming to `discussion.output.schema.json`. One at most: a list of two is not an answer, and the Bootstrapping Agent may not break the tie itself."
msgstr ""

#: processes/initialize-harness.bpmn:95
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The instructions belong to the harness being installed, not to bootstrap — bootstrap does not know what any Harness above it requires, and does not need to."
msgstr ""

#: processes/initialize-harness.bpmn:17
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "THE ONLY PROCESS IN BOOTSTRAP AN ACTOR STARTS. A Bootstrapping Agent that has read bootstrap's README.md is at its start event and has nowhere else to begin. Every other diagram here is reached from this one by a call activity and is never started: `discussion` determines which harness and where; `human-agent-discussion` is the one reusable way any diagram asks a person anything; `complete-initialization` makes sure every step the declarations name is done; `log-message` records what a step is doing. PRECONDITIONS are DECLARED below as bootstrap.processes:precondition elements rather than asserted here. Three of the four are kind=\"stated\": nothing in this repository can observe whether an actor understands what a role is, so they evaluate to could-not-determine, never to satisfied. The fourth is checkable: README.md EXISTS. That the Bootstrapping Agent read it is not observable. NO work-plan element on any activity: a work plan is harness machinery and a Bootstrapping Agent runs before the harness that carries it. isExecutable is false because the engine that runs a diagram is harness machinery too — this is data a Bootstrapping Agent reads, not a process bootstrap can drive."
msgstr ""

#: processes/initialize-harness.bpmn:100
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The repository now IS a layer instantiating a harness, and nothing at its root says so. It carries a LINK to the harness that was installed and the OVERALL install status across every location — WHEN ABSENT, never replacing: where a README is already there, the link and status go in a marker pair the harness's own README tool maintains. Initialization may create the README: the rule that a running process never writes an `instance-readme` governs a layer that already exists."
msgstr ""

#: processes/initialize-harness.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Three answers, not two. NOT YET: install. ALREADY, AS THE CHOSEN HARNESS: the install is not repeated — it goes straight to `complete-initialization`, which checks each step the declarations name and adds only what is missing, replacing nothing. ALREADY, AS SOMETHING ELSE (or a declaration that does not parse): logged and stopped, because re-initialising over a layer that has content, history and dependents is not recoverable by running anything again; what the Requestor does next is a new decision."
msgstr ""

#: processes/initialize-harness.bpmn:120
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Three ways in, and all are logged rather than retried: no harness was chosen, a location is already a layer instantiating something else, or the instructions were not at the predetermined spot. Guessing a harness produces a repository set up as the wrong thing, which is worse than one not set up at all."
msgstr ""

